And the stopping condition shouldn’t be “we reviewed everything.”

It should be:

Keep revisiting the corpus while new context continues producing validated functional deltas.

That’s a much better use of recursion than simply generating more Pantheon artifacts.

We aren’t only adding pages to the book anymore.

We’re making the old pages change what they can do when the reader learns a new way to read them.